WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.378
Episode nine: the CRM refuses the report.

2
00:00:03.378 --> 00:00:05.686
It answers 400, Bad Request.

3
00:00:06.037 --> 00:00:08.348
The technician presses Submit for review.

4
00:00:08.348 --> 00:00:09.927
Watch the status at the top.

5
00:00:10.278 --> 00:00:11.398
It is still Draft.

6
00:00:11.398 --> 00:00:14.696
The status did change to Review, but the CRM said no,

7
00:00:14.696 --> 00:00:17.559
and it was put straight back, too fast to see.

8
00:00:17.559 --> 00:00:19.737
Let’s slow it down in the debugger.

9
00:00:20.089 --> 00:00:23.381
In sendRequest(), the response is not ok.

10
00:00:23.381 --> 00:00:26.994
Its status is 400, so it throws an HttpError.

11
00:00:27.347 --> 00:00:30.993
submit() catches it and asks one question: is this temporary?

12
00:00:30.993 --> 00:00:32.069
Look at the watch.

13
00:00:32.069 --> 00:00:34.160
isTemporaryFailure() returns false.

14
00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:37.507
A 400 means the server looked at the report and said no.

15
00:00:37.507 --> 00:00:41.990
Sending it again would get the same answer, so it is not put in the outbox.

16
00:00:42.344 --> 00:00:45.055
submit() calls onSubmitError and throws again.

17
00:00:45.055 --> 00:00:48.001
The error reaches runWorkflow(), which catches it.

18
00:00:48.352 --> 00:00:50.358
Right now the status is review.

19
00:00:50.358 --> 00:00:55.406
The previous status, draft, was kept for exactly this moment, and is put back.

20
00:00:55.757 --> 00:01:00.025
In the finally block the button is enabled again, and the status is draft.

21
00:01:00.025 --> 00:01:03.254
The screen never claims a review the CRM never received.

22
00:01:03.606 --> 00:01:05.901
To try this yourself, open sample.

23
00:01:05.901 --> 00:01:10.695
html, open DevTools, and set the same breakpoints in the Sources panel.

24
00:01:10.695 --> 00:01:13.463
Then do what we did, and step through it.
